          "publishedAt": "2026-11-03T21:24:01Z",
          "channelId": "UCbyLx6Rf3iWww4bPZJ2oo2A",
          "title": "How the Black Death Spread Across Medieval Europe",
          "description": "The Black Death spread across connected medieval trade routes, reaching ports and cities far from its point of arrival. This film follows how the plague moved through Europe, how communities tried to limit its spread, and how trade and daily life continued under pressure.\n\nFrom busy ports to Dubrovnik’s 30-day isolation rule, see how medieval towns tried to manage danger while depending on the movement of people and goods.\n\nChapters\n00:00 The 181 Coins at East Smithfield\n00:54 Trade Across Medieval Europe\n01:21 The Plague Reaches New Cities\n02:10 Illness and Care\n03:32 Choices in Florence\n04:54 Order, Fear, and Loss at East Smithfield\n06:05 Labor Shortages and New Laws\n07:37 Dubrovnik and Isolation\n09:05 London and the Earlier Evidence\n10:29 The Work That Continued\n\n#BlackDeath #MedievalHistory #LondonHistory #Plague #MedievalEurope #MedievalTrade #Quarantine #EastSmithfield #Dubrovnik",
