          "channelId": "UCbyLx6Rf3iWww4bPZJ2oo2A",
          "title": "Pompeii Wasn’t Buried by Lava. What Actually Destroyed It?",
          "description": "Was Pompeii destroyed by a flood of lava? The film traces a different sequence: a towering eruption column sent pumice toward the city, earthquakes shook buildings, and later pyroclastic flows swept in. It follows the eruption from the first falling stones to the morning after, while distinguishing Pompeii from nearby Herculaneum and Stabiae.\n\nChapters:\n00:00 The final hours begin\n00:32 A rain of stones\n01:39 Everyday life in Pompeii\n02:44 Earthquakes before the eruption\n03:25 Vesuvius erupts\n04:08 Pumice falls on Pompeii\n05:08 The people who escaped\n05:35 Pliny the Elder’s voyage\n06:32 Darkness and earthquakes\n07:40 Pliny the Younger’s escape\n07:59 Herculaneum and the first flows\n08:45 Morning in Pompeii\n09:12 A lull before the next danger\n09:33 The flow reaches Pompeii\n10:58 Pliny’s letters and the aftermath\n11:44 Excavation and plaster casts\n12:57 The lives Pompeii preserved\n\n#Pompeii #MountVesuvius #VesuviusEruption #79AD #AncientRome #RomanHistory #AncientHistory #HistoryDocumentary #PyroclasticFlow #VolcanicEruption #VolcanicAsh #Pumice #Herculaneum #Stabiae #PlinyTheYounger #PlinyTheElder #Archaeology #PlasterCasts",
